---
import DocsLayout from '@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { DocsTable } from '@/molecules/DocComponents/DocComponents';
import MermaidDiagram from '@/components/MermaidDiagram.astro';

const COMPONENTS = [
  ['Manager', 'Product control plane', 'Users, organizations, GitHub connections, runtime identity, broker, operations, hook ingress'],
  ['Coder', 'Execution control plane', 'Templates, builds, workspace agents, and workspace lifecycle'],
  ['Nexus', 'Tenant controller', 'Issue sync, scheduling, reconciliation, agent hooks, and A2A relay'],
  ['Forge, Sentinel, Vessel, Lore', 'Tenant workers', 'Scoped work in separate disposable Coder workspaces'],
  ['PostgreSQL', 'Manager system of record', 'Ownership, operation leases, workspace credentials, and broker leases'],
  ['Redis', 'Tenant coordination store', 'Tickets, worker slots, agent heartbeats, A2A evidence, and hook audit'],
];
---

<DocsLayout breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Docs', href: '/docs' }, { label: 'Architecture', href: '/docs/architecture' }, { label: 'Big Picture' }]}>
  <h1>The big picture</h1>
  <p>OpenFlows Manager is the trusted product control plane. Coder provides workspace execution. Nexus is the controller inside one tenant's runtime, and workers execute ticket-scoped tasks in separate workspaces.</p>
  <MermaidDiagram title="The product control plane provisions and supports a tenant runtime" source={`flowchart TB
    user["Signed-in user"] --> manager["OpenFlows Manager"]
    manager --> postgres[(PostgreSQL)]
    manager --> coder["Coder"]
    manager --> github["GitHub App"]
    coder --> nexus["Nexus controller"]
    coder --> workers["Worker workspaces"]
    nexus <--> redis[("Tenant Redis")]
    workers <--> redis`} />
  <DocsTable headers={['Component', 'Boundary', 'Responsibility']} rows={COMPONENTS} />
  <h2 id="flow">From organization to agent work</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>A user signs into Manager, creates an organization, and connects a GitHub App installation.</li>
    <li>Manager provisions a tenant and Nexus using durable operations and pinned Coder templates.</li>
    <li>Nexus registers a runtime session, synchronizes repository work using a brokered installation token, and asks Manager for workers.</li>
    <li>Manager authorizes and creates workers in Coder. The workers register their own scoped runtime sessions.</li>
    <li>Forge and Sentinel exchange verification requests through the Nexus A2A relay, with evidence stored in tenant Redis.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>See <a href="/docs/architecture/manager-runtime">Manager Runtime</a> for the lifecycle and <a href="/docs/architecture/credentials">Credentials and Trust</a> for the exact authority boundaries.</p>
</DocsLayout>
